<script type="application/json" id="mq-examples">{{ meetingQualityPage.examples | json | safe }}</script>
<main class="mq-page">
  <div class="mq-hero-shell">
    <nav class="mq-wrap mq-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Meeting quality check</span></nav>
    <section class="mq-wrap mq-hero" aria-labelledby="mq-title">
      <div><p class="mq-eyebrow">Free B2B appointment-setting performance calculator</p><h1 id="mq-title">Are your booked meetings turning into <span>sales opportunities?</span></h1><p class="mq-lead">Enter your campaign numbers. See how many meetings happened, how many sales accepted and how many became opportunities, with practical questions to investigate next.</p><div class="mq-actions"><a class="mq-button" href="#mq-checker">Check My Meeting Results <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a><a class="mq-text-link" href="#mq-example">See an example <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="mq-micro">Free. No email required. Results stay in your browser.</p><p class="mq-byline">Written by <a href="{{ authors.harjSingh.url }}">{{ authors.harjSingh.name }}</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Updated <time datetime="2026-10-15">October 15, 2026</time></p></div>
      <aside class="mq-hero-sheet" aria-label="Illustrative campaign progression"><div class="mq-sheet-label"><span>FOLLOW THE MEETING</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><ol class="mq-example-stages"><li><span>Booked</span><strong>8</strong></li><li><span>Held</span><strong>6</strong></li><li><span>Sales accepted</span><strong>4</strong></li><li><span>Created an opportunity</span><strong>2</strong></li></ol><p>One illustrative group of bookings.<br>No monthly target or performance promise.</p></aside>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section id="mq-checker" class="mq-checker-section" aria-labelledby="mq-checker-title"><div class="mq-wrap">
    <div class="mq-heading"><div><p class="mq-eyebrow">01 / Your campaign numbers</p><h2 id="mq-checker-title">Start with one group<br>of bookings.</h2></div><p>Follow the same bookings through each stage. Choose a completed group where possible. Leave a stage blank if you do not track it.</p></div>
    <noscript><p class="mq-notice">Enable JavaScript to calculate your results. The definitions, formulas, worked example and guidance below are available without it.</p></noscript>
    <div class="mq-workspace">
      <div id="mq-inputs" class="mq-input-panel" role="group" aria-labelledby="mq-checker-title" data-clarity-mask="true">
        <div class="mq-field-grid">{% for field in meetingQualityPage.fields %}<div class="mq-field"><label for="mq-{{ field.key }}"><span class="mq-field-index">{{ field.number }}</span>{{ field.label }}</label><input id="mq-{{ field.key }}" name="{{ field.key }}" type="text" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" maxlength="7" autocomplete="off" placeholder="e.g. {{ field.placeholder }}" aria-describedby="mq-{{ field.key }}-help"{% if field.key == 'booked' %} required{% endif %}><p id="mq-{{ field.key }}-help">{{ field.help }}</p>{% if field.key != 'booked' %}<label class="mq-unknown-label" for="mq-{{ field.key }}-unknown"><input type="checkbox" id="mq-{{ field.key }}-unknown" data-mq-unknown="{{ field.key }}">I don’t track this</label>{% endif %}</div>{% endfor %}</div>
        <div class="mq-field mq-outcomes-field"><label for="mq-outcomes">Have these bookings had time to progress?</label><select id="mq-outcomes" aria-describedby="mq-outcomes-help"><option value="unknown">Not sure yet</option><option value="complete">Yes, the outcomes are complete</option><option value="pending">Still in progress</option></select><p id="mq-outcomes-help">Allow for your normal sales cycle. Future meetings and pending decisions are not failed outcomes.</p></div>
        <p class="mq-input-guidance">Enter whole numbers from 0 to 1,000,000. Later stages must be part of the same earlier group.</p>
        <div class="mq-actions"><button id="mq-check" type="button" class="mq-button" disabled>Check My Meeting Results <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><button id="mq-clear" type="button" class="mq-text-button">Clear entries</button></div><div id="mq-errors" class="mq-notice" role="alert" hidden></div><p id="mq-status" class="mq-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p><p class="mq-privacy">Your figures are not submitted to CallTeam or attached to a booking. <a href="#mq-privacy">How your numbers are handled.</a></p>
      </div>
      <aside class="mq-input-aside"><p class="mq-eyebrow">What you leave with</p><h3>A clearer view of<br>what happens next.</h3><ul class="mq-benefits"><li>Your conversion rates, with the counts behind them.</li><li>Questions matched to your results and missing information.</li><li>A checklist you can copy or download for your team.</li></ul><div class="mq-samples"><p>Try a practical example</p>{% for example in meetingQualityPage.examples %}<button type="button" data-mq-example="{{ example.id }}" class="mq-sample">{{ example.label }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>{% endfor %}<small>Illustrative inputs. Each example uses the same calculations as your own entries.</small></div></aside>
    </div>

    <section id="mq-results" class="mq-results" aria-labelledby="mq-results-title" tabindex="-1" data-clarity-mask="true" hidden>
      <div class="mq-result-heading"><div><p id="mq-result-mode" class="mq-eyebrow">Your numbers / Your next steps</p><h2 id="mq-results-title">Your meeting results.</h2></div><span id="mq-completeness" class="mq-status-label"></span></div>
      <div id="mq-stages" class="mq-result-stages" aria-label="Your meeting counts"></div><div id="mq-metrics" class="mq-metrics" aria-label="Calculated conversion rates"></div>
      <div class="mq-result-detail"><div class="mq-focus"><p class="mq-eyebrow">Where to start</p><h3 id="mq-focus-title"></h3><p id="mq-focus-summary"></p><ul id="mq-checks"></ul><a id="mq-resource" class="mq-text-link" href="/articles/cold-calling-metrics-campaign-quality/">Read the campaign metrics guide</a></div><aside class="mq-context"><h3>Read the figures in context.</h3><ul id="mq-notes"></ul><p>The counts show progression. They do not establish why a meeting stopped or who caused it.</p></aside></div>
      <div class="mq-save"><button id="mq-copy" type="button" class="mq-button mq-button-secondary">Copy Results and Checklist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button id="mq-download" type="button" class="mq-text-button">Download .txt <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></button><p id="mq-copy-status" class="mq-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="mq-copy-fallback-wrap" hidden><label for="mq-copy-fallback">Select and copy your results</label><textarea id="mq-copy-fallback" readonly rows="10"></textarea></div></div>
      <div class="mq-result-cta"><div><h3>Put these results to work.</h3><p>Bring your checklist. Let’s review the targeting, qualification and sales handoff your campaign needs.</p></div><a class="mq-button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-mq-booking>Review My Campaign <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </section>
  </div></section>

  <section id="mq-definitions" class="mq-definitions-section" aria-labelledby="mq-definitions-title"><div class="mq-wrap">
    <div class="mq-heading"><div><p class="mq-eyebrow">02 / Count the same thing</p><h2 id="mq-definitions-title">Booked, held, accepted.<br>What is the difference?</h2></div><p>A useful report needs agreed definitions. These are the counting rules used in this calculator.</p></div><div class="mq-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Meeting stage definitions" tabindex="0"><table class="mq-table"><caption class="sr-only">Definitions for the B2B meeting quality check</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">What it means</th><th scope="col">How to count it</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for item in meetingQualityPage.definitions %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ item.name }}</th><td>{{ item.definition }}</td><td>{{ item.rule }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div><p class="mq-section-note">Do not mix this month’s bookings with opportunities from an older campaign. Read our <a href="/articles/cold-calling-metrics-campaign-quality/">guide to measuring cold calling campaign quality</a> for the wider reporting approach.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section id="mq-example" class="mq-example-section" aria-labelledby="mq-example-title"><div class="mq-wrap">
    <div class="mq-heading"><div><p class="mq-eyebrow">03 / A small worked example</p><h2 id="mq-example-title">Eight bookings.<br>Follow what happened.</h2></div><p>Imagine one completed group: 8 booked, 6 held, 4 accepted and 2 that created opportunities. These are illustrative figures, with no assumed monthly delivery volume.</p></div>
    <div class="mq-example-grid"><div class="mq-formulas"><div><span>Held rate</span><strong>6 ÷ 8 × 100 = <em>75%</em></strong></div><div><span>Sales acceptance rate</span><strong>4 ÷ 6 × 100 = <em>66.7%</em></strong></div><div><span>Held meeting-to-opportunity rate</span><strong>2 ÷ 6 × 100 = <em>33.3%</em></strong></div><div><span>Booked meeting-to-opportunity rate</span><strong>2 ÷ 8 × 100 = <em>25%</em></strong></div></div><aside class="mq-example-reading"><p class="mq-eyebrow">How to read this example</p><h3>The next question comes<br>from the missing context.</h3><p>Two meetings separate each stage, so there is no single largest numerical drop. Check the reasons behind each transition before choosing what to change.</p><p>For the two bookings that were not held, review the recorded outcome. For the two held meetings sales did not accept, read the rejection reasons. For the two accepted meetings without an opportunity, review the discovery notes and next steps.</p><p class="mq-small">With six held meetings, one different outcome moves a held-meeting conversion rate by 16.7 percentage points. Treat a small group as a starting point for investigation.</p><button type="button" class="mq-text-button" data-mq-example="small">Run these numbers <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></aside></div>
  </div></section>

  <section id="mq-next-checks" aria-labelledby="mq-next-checks-title"><div class="mq-wrap mq-guidance-grid"><div><p class="mq-eyebrow">04 / Use the result</p><h2 id="mq-next-checks-title">What should you<br>check first?</h2><p>Use the observed stage difference to choose a question. Use your campaign records to answer it.</p><p>Keep customer fit, the contact’s relevance, a real reason to talk and the meeting’s purpose explicit. CallTeam’s <a href="/articles/what-makes-b2b-appointment-qualified-practical-standard/">qualified appointment standard</a> explains how to separate confirmed information from unknowns.</p></div><ol class="mq-investigations">{% for item in meetingQualityPage.investigations %}<li><span aria-hidden="true">0{{ loop.index }}</span><div><h3>{{ item.title }}</h3><p>{{ item.text }}</p><a href="{{ item.href }}" class="mq-text-link">{{ item.label }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></li>{% endfor %}</ol></div></section>

  <section class="mq-proof-section" aria-labelledby="mq-proof-title"><div class="mq-wrap mq-proof-grid"><div><p class="mq-eyebrow">05 / Real CallTeam campaign work</p><h2 id="mq-proof-title">The work behind<br>a useful sales meeting.</h2><p>CallTeam’s published SaaS demo campaign describes the targeting, conversations and qualification behind booked demos, followed by opportunities and customer outcomes.</p><p>That campaign provides context for the process. It is separate from this calculator’s illustrative figures and is not a benchmark for your results.</p><a class="mq-text-link" href="/case-studies/saas-demo-appointment-setting/">Read the SaaS demo case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><aside><p class="mq-eyebrow">A conversation sales can use</p><blockquote>Give the sales team the reason for the meeting, the prospect’s context and the next step they agreed to.</blockquote><a class="mq-text-link" href="/services/b2b-appointment-setting/">How CallTeam runs appointment setting <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></aside></div></section>

  <section class="mq-faq-section" aria-labelledby="mq-faq-title"><div class="mq-wrap mq-faq-grid"><div><p class="mq-eyebrow">06 / Questions about your results</p><h2 id="mq-faq-title">Make the numbers<br>useful.</h2><p>Clear definitions make campaign reviews more productive. Here is how this meeting conversion calculator handles common questions.</p></div><div class="mq-faqs">{% for faq in meetingQualityPage.faqs %}<details{% if loop.last %} id="mq-privacy"{% endif %}><summary>{{ faq.q }}</summary><p>{{ faq.a }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div></div></section>

  <section class="mq-final-section" aria-labelledby="mq-final-title"><div class="mq-wrap mq-final-grid"><div><p class="mq-eyebrow">07 / Your next campaign decision</p><h2 id="mq-final-title">Before you buy more meetings,<br>make the next ones count.</h2><p>Bring your results. Let’s talk through who you are targeting, what makes a meeting qualified and how the conversation reaches your sales team.</p><div class="mq-actions"><a class="mq-button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-mq-booking>Review My Appointment-Setting Campaign <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><aside><p class="mq-eyebrow">Planning what comes next?</p><a href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/" class="mq-next-link"><strong>See how we’d run your campaign.</strong><span>Explore an approach for your market and buyer. ↗</span></a><a href="/b2b-lead-generation-roi-calculator/" class="mq-next-link"><strong>Calculate your campaign ROI.</strong><span>Explore costs and potential returns using your assumptions. ↗</span></a></aside></div></section>
</main>
